window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-d5a186b7366ebd04"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"codex-security\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"codex-securitycodex\">Codex Security（Codex 安全）</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>Codex Security 会检查代码中的安全漏洞，并提供证据，供你调查这些漏洞并着手修复。请根据代码所在位置以及你希望如何审核结果，选择运行方式。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-where-to-start\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">选择开始方式</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>使用方式</th> <th>适用情况</th> <th>从这里开始</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Codex Security Cloud</td> <td>在 Codex 云端扫描已连接的 GitHub 代码库，或监控新提交。</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-10cdc56de63926b8\">云端设置</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Codex Security plugin</td> <td>在 Codex 中扫描本地代码库，并交互式处理发现的问题。</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-bec1e26cb654a758\">运行首次本地扫描</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Codex Security CLI</td> <td>在终端中运行可重复的扫描，或将检查加入 CI。</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-1716f9f1a07bca7e\">CLI 快速入门</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Codex Security SDK</td> <td>在应用或开发者工具中运行扫描并处理结果。</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-13b97f7316a6bfd5\">SDK 指南</a></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>首次进行本地扫描时，建议使用插件。在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中选择 <strong>Codex</strong>，安装 <strong>Codex Security</strong>，然后在侧边栏打开 <strong>Security</strong>。<a href=\"#/article/a-8486fe00c240100d\">Security 工作台</a>会保存扫描和发现结果，方便后续审核。你也可以在 Codex CLI 中使用该插件。</p> <p>Codex Security CLI 和 SDK 通过公开的 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex-security\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">@openai/codex-security 软件包（需联网）</a>分发。使用 OpenAI 推理能力进行扫描需要拥有 Codex Security 访问权限。运行环境和身份验证要求请参阅相应的快速入门指南。</p> <p>Codex Security Cloud 是一个独立插件，目前在网页端和桌面应用中以研究预览形式提供。它要求你拥有工作区访问权限、连接 GitHub，并使用兼容的 Codex 云环境。设置过程中，你可以连接代码库并创建环境。</p> <blockquote> <p>截图未离线保存: Codex Security Cloud 概览，显示代码库数量、安全发现项的状态，以及需要关注的发现项</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> 跟踪不同代码库中的未解决发现和修复情况。本示例中的代码库、发现内容和数量均为虚构。 </figcaption> <p>有关发布在 GitHub pull request 中的安全审查，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-862c857e0358aa15\">Security Review</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-the-next-task\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">选择下一项任务</h2> <p>完成本地扫描后，请先审核扫描范围和发现结果，再决定下一步怎么做。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>任务</th> <th>指南</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>将扫描范围限定到某个服务，或补充安全背景信息</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-52ffdad46ad27a2b\">运行安全扫描</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>对同一代码库或文件夹重复进行审核</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-03d337741f7199f7\">运行深度扫描</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>检查 pull request、commit 或本地差异</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-06694345b68735af\">审核代码更改</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>评估其他扫描器或问题跟踪器发现的问题</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-3623d131a0f26273\">分类处理待办问题</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>生成补丁并检查其是否修复了问题</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\">修复并验证发现项</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>分享结果或分配修复工作</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-2908d6b44ee04c2d\">导出并跟踪发现项</a></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>如需自动化，请使用 CLI 指南<a href=\"#/article/a-0462b3e291010c32\">批量扫描代码库</a>，或<a href=\"#/article/a-8d926b82884d5f99\">在 CI 中运行扫描</a>。命令和默认值请查阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34\">CLI 参考</a>。</p> <p>Codex Security 扫描的是应用程序代码。有关控制 Codex 自身权限和沙盒的设置，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">代理审批与安全</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"codex-security\">Codex Security</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Codex Security reviews code for vulnerabilities and reports evidence you can use to investigate and fix them. Choose how to run it based on where your code lives and how you want to review the results.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-where-to-start\">Choose where to start</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Use</th> <th>When you want to</th> <th>Start here</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Codex Security Cloud</td> <td>Scan connected GitHub repositories in Codex cloud or monitor new commits.</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-10cdc56de63926b8\">Cloud setup</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Codex Security plugin</td> <td>Scan a local repository in Codex and work through findings interactively.</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-bec1e26cb654a758\">Run your first local scan</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Codex Security CLI</td> <td>Run repeatable terminal scans or add checks to CI.</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-1716f9f1a07bca7e\">CLI quickstart</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Codex Security SDK</td> <td>Run scans and handle results in an application or developer tool.</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-13b97f7316a6bfd5\">SDK guide</a></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>For your first local scan, use the plugin. In the ChatGPT desktop app, select <strong>Codex</strong>, install <strong>Codex Security</strong>, and open <strong>Security</strong> in the sidebar. The <a href=\"#/article/a-8486fe00c240100d\">Security workbench</a> keeps saved scans and findings available for review. You can also use the plugin in Codex CLI.</p> <p>The Codex Security CLI and SDK are distributed in the public <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex-security\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">@openai/codex-security package (online)</a>. Scans using OpenAI inference require Codex Security access. See each quickstart for its runtime and authentication requirements.</p> <p>Codex Security Cloud is a separate plugin, available in research preview on the web and in the desktop app. It requires workspace access, a GitHub connection, and a compatible Codex cloud environment. You can connect the repository and create an environment during setup.</p> <blockquote> <p>Screenshot not stored offline: Codex Security Cloud overview with repository counts, finding statuses, and findings that need attention</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> Track open findings and fixes across repositories. This example uses fictional repositories, findings, and counts. </figcaption> <p>For security reviews posted to GitHub pull requests, see <a href=\"#/article/a-862c857e0358aa15\">Security Review</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-the-next-task\">Choose the next task</h2> <p>After a local scan, review its scope and findings before deciding what to do next.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Task</th> <th>Guide</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Focus a scan on a service or add security context</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-52ffdad46ad27a2b\">Run a security scan</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Run repeated reviews of the same repository or folder</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-03d337741f7199f7\">Run a deep scan</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Check a pull request, commit, or local diff</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-06694345b68735af\">Review code changes</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Assess findings from another scanner or issue tracker</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-3623d131a0f26273\">Triage a backlog</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Generate a patch and check whether it fixes the issue</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\">Fix and verify findings</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Share results or assign remediation work</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-2908d6b44ee04c2d\">Export and track findings</a></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>For automation, use the CLI guides to <a href=\"#/article/a-0462b3e291010c32\">scan repositories in bulk</a> or <a href=\"#/article/a-8d926b82884d5f99\">run scans in CI</a>. Look up commands and defaults in the <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34\">CLI reference</a>.</p> <p>Codex Security scans application code. For permissions and sandbox controls that govern Codex itself, see <a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">Agent approvals and security</a>.</p>"};
